msgid "ChatGPT Model:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:260
msgid "If you want to use gpt-4o, you must subscribe to chatgpt plus. The model gpt4-o is a better version of gpt-4, with faster speed and lower cost."
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:271
msgid "Chatbot Name:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:282
msgid "Chatbot Logo:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:319
msgid "Temperature:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:338
msgid "The temperature parameter influences the level of randomness in the output generated by the model. When the temperature is lowered, the model becomes more confident but also tends to repeat similar responses. On the other hand, raising the temperature value increases its creativity but also makes its outputs more unpredictable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:349
msgid "Max used contexts:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:373
msgid "The maximum number of contexts that the model can use to generate an answer. The higher this parameter is, the more information the model can use to generate an answer. However, increasing this value also increases the risk of generating irrelevant answers. The default value is 3, which is a good balance between relevance and creativity. If you want to prioritize relevance, you can lower this value to 1. If you want to prioritize creativity, you can increase this value to 10."
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:384
msgid "Similarity threshold:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:409
msgid "This determines the maximum difference allowed between the most likely context to be used, and other contexts. Here is an example: if the similarity threshold is set to 5, the model will only consider contexts that are at most 5% less likely than the most likely context. This parameter is useful to prevent the model from generating irrelevant answers when the most likely context is not relevant. The default value is 5, which is a good balance between relevance and creativity. If you want to prioritize relevance, you can lower this value to 1. If you want to prioritize creativity, you can increase this value to 10."
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:420
msgid "Precision threshold:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/config/wdgpt-config-general-settings.php:445
msgid "The minimum precision required for a context to be considered eligible determines its relevance to the answer. By increasing this value, the system prioritizes more precise and relevant contexts, potentially leading to better results. However, there is a trade-off, as a higher threshold also increases the risk of not generating an answer if the context or the prompt are not sufficiently relevant."
msgstr ""

